  "title": "Mexico captures top cartel boss 'El Chapo Isidro', FBI's most-wanted fugitive",
  "summary": "Mexico captured Fausto Isidro Meza Flores, a Mexican drug lord known as 'El Chapo Isidro', in Sinaloa, marking a significant victory for the Mexican government. The capture was aided by intelligence from the Trump administration and led to increased pressure from the FBI, who have called him one of the most dangerous fugitives.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Meza Flores, known as 'El Chapo Isidro', was captured in Sinaloa by Mexican authorities aided by intelligence from the Trump administration.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The FBI and Mexico's government have called him one of the top 10 most wanted fugitives with a USD 5 million reward for information.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Meza Flores led the Beltran Leyva cartel and his own group, the Meza-Flores Transnational Criminal Organization, and is linked to drug trafficking, kidnapping, and extortion.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
